  "description": "S7.1.3v2: typed cold stores retain the checked error boundary. Tune13 typed array stores retain native indexed arithmetic and type-preserving builtin results. 2026-09-17 (T28-7): the indices are parameters; literal indices into these fixed-length locals are proven in bounds and have neither a checked store nor an index multiply (tune28_fixed_length_index). T29-5 (2026-09-17): a non-null int value takes the compact COW store (array_num_set_cow_idx) on a statically proven int[] root, as bool and non-null float values already did; out-of-range stores still raise through fn_array_set. Typed-performance audit: abs keeps the integer lane and its poison/null sentinels directly (S7.10.5v3, D2.2.2).",
